WEBVTT

00:00:10.102 --> 00:00:11.988
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> What are you doing in the US?

00:00:11.989 --> 00:00:13.272
<v><b>Cara:</b></v> I’m visiting from England.

00:00:13.273 --> 00:00:15.174
I’m just on holiday for one week.

00:00:15.175 --> 00:00:18.949
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> Was there anything that surprised you about the US when you arrived?

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:22.337
<v><b>Cara:</b></v> Um, I was quite surprised by how busy New York is.

00:00:22.338 --> 00:00:25.294
Although I suppose I shouldn’t have been because it’s one of the biggest cities.

00:00:25.562 --> 00:00:28.315
Um, and there are lots of nice places to eat as well.

00:00:36.384 --> 00:00:38.550
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> How do people in your country drive?

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:40.640
<v><b>Madeleine:</b></v> I think it depends where you are.

00:00:40.641 --> 00:00:44.068
Where I live in Oregon, everything is very safe, much slower,

00:00:44.069 --> 00:00:48.160
but in New York City everything is very fast, very dangerous.

00:00:49.564 --> 00:00:52.920
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> Are you a typical driver for where you live for Oregon?

00:00:53.314 --> 00:00:55.847
<v><b>Madeleine:</b></v> I would say so, I drive, I’m a very cautious driver.

00:01:02.336 --> 00:01:05.329
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> Do you have any ambitions for this year?

00:01:06.139 --> 00:01:12.788
<v><b>Chris:</b></v> Um, yes, I’d like to visit my daughter in Australia, and also plan towards my retirement.

00:01:14.359 --> 00:01:16.285
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> Do you think you’re going to do them?

00:01:17.945 --> 00:01:22.679
<v><b>Chris:</b></v> Certainly the planning, whether or not I achieve the visit is something else.

00:01:28.802 --> 00:01:31.960
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> Have you ever seen a movie more than three times?

00:01:32.089 --> 00:01:36.897
<v><b>Susan:</b></v> I’ve seen <i>Casablanca</i> many times, and I still think it’s one of the best films made.

00:01:37.344 --> 00:01:38.822
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> What do you like about it?

00:01:39.387 --> 00:01:42.480
<v><b>Susan:</b></v> Everything. I like the direction, the lighting.

00:01:43.046 --> 00:01:44.920
I like each of the stars.

00:01:45.144 --> 00:01:47.881
The story has romance and intrigue.

00:01:48.199 --> 00:01:50.479
I like stories about World War II.

00:01:50.953 --> 00:01:55.099
Um, I love Claude Raines, Humphrey Bogart.

00:01:55.567 --> 00:01:58.506
There’s like nothing not to like in that movie.

00:02:04.052 --> 00:02:05.978
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> What phone do you have?

00:02:06.398 --> 00:02:07.724
<v><b>Martin:</b></v> I have an iPhone.

00:02:07.844 --> 00:02:09.161
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> How old is it?

00:02:09.355 --> 00:02:13.147
<v><b>Martin:</b></v> I believe, I believe my iPhone is now two years old.

00:02:13.493 --> 00:02:15.731
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> How often do you change phones?

00:02:17.053 --> 00:02:20.039
<v><b>Martin:</b></v> I change phones maybe every three years.

00:02:20.183 --> 00:02:22.009
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> What do you use it for the most?

00:02:23.235 --> 00:02:25.641
<v><b>Martin:</b></v> I mostly use my phone for social media.